"epic sort" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-sort&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-sort&gt; element: the Epics page's sort buttons, A to Z or newest first, for every list on the page.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph><text code>&lt;epic-sort&gt;</> is the Epics page's pair of sort buttons, A–Z and Date: how every <link target="src-spell-epic-src-docs-epic-list-html" link="/epic-list"><text code>&lt;epic-list&gt;</></> on the page sorts the cards in each group.</>
	<list bulleted>
		<item>The one in use is pressed, and remembered in this browser.</>
		<item>The groups stay where they are: only the cards inside each move.</>
	</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone changing the Epics page.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Status: <label size="mini" color="green">built</> (epic <text code>epic-engine</> P3), in the <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-list" link="/epic/src/components/epic-list/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-list/" code>epic-list</></> family, with <text code>&lt;epic-list&gt;</>, <text code>&lt;epic-card&gt;</> and <text code>&lt;epic-sort&gt;</>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-list-epicsort-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicSort.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicSort.en.ts" code>EpicSort.en.ts</></></>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-list-epicsort-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicSort.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicSort.tsx" code>EpicSort.tsx</></>.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<example "Example">
			<html>
				<epic-sort></epic-sort>
			</html>
		</example>
		<text paragraph>The same choice as the Epics page's, and <link target="src-spell-epic-src-docs-epic-list-html" link="/epic-list">epic-list's example</>'s: they share it.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>Nobody writes it: the docs runtime puts one in the Epics page's header, beside New epic, when the page has an <text code>&lt;epic-list&gt;</> (<link target="src-spell-epic-src-tools-assets-spell-doc-runtime-js" link="/epic/src/tools/_assets/spell-doc-runtime.js"><text title="epic/src/tools/_assets/spell-doc-runtime.js" code>wireEpicSort()</></>).</>
	</>

